  "explanation": {
    "en": "〜本 (ほん) is the counter for long, thin objects such as bottles, pencils, and umbrellas. The pronunciation changes depending on the number.\n\nKey points:\n• 1本 = いっぽん\n• 2本 = にほん\n• 3本 = さんぼん\n• 4本 = よんほん\n• 5本 = ごほん\n• 6本 = ろっぽん\n• 7本 = ななほん\n• 8本 = はっぽん\n• 9本 = きゅうほん\n• 10本 = じゅっぽん\n\nExample: “ペンを三本買いました” means “I bought three pens.”\n\nRemember the sound changes (hon → bon/pon) for certain numbers.\n\nPractice by counting pens, bottles, or chopsticks with 本.",
    "ja": ""
  },
